From 3ea4c2710d6f5d5b71e76238cf3308b797746ec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:58:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: index V2 blocks whose children precede their
 in-block parents

The V2 index service stopped at the first block with chained spends
("invalid V2 index transition: missing coin", regtest height 103 in the
parity harness). The ABC host confirms blocks in canonical (txid) order,
so a transaction can come before the in-block parent whose output it
spends. Connect resolved and applied transactions strictly in block order
and required every spent coin to exist already. The txids were correct:
the missing coin was an output of a later transaction in the same block.

Connect and the undo validation of disconnect now resolve, spend and plan
asset events in a parents-first order: each in-block parent before its
children, otherwise block order, so a topologically ordered block is
processed exactly as before. Positions, receipts and explorer records keep
block order. Two read and planning checks assumed that an in-block
creation always has a lower position than its spender (explorer inputs) or
that an asset's first event has the lowest position (asset summaries); they
now accept any other position in the same block. A dependency cycle still
fails as a missing coin.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/026)
